{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified VAI 64 days after the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D4"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's history shows an earlier shortage of indigotindisulfonate sodium first posted on 2022-08-23, since resolved, and the drug is not on FDA's current shortage list as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D5"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product label for NDC 81284031505 names CENEXI (FEI 3007250542) as the registered plant for analysis, manufacture, and pack.",
      "cites": ["E10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1245208 at that plant ended 2022-10-26 and was classified VAI — 64 days after FDA posted the shortage on 2022-08-23.",
      "cites": ["D4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Earlier inspections at the same plant include an OAI classification in 2015 (inspection 924508) and VAI classifications in 2012, 2016, and 2018.",
      "cites": ["E4", "E6", "E7", "E8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 31 units at 4.4 per day for 7.1 days on hand; Corvale General holds 64 units at 4.3 per day for 14.8 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The top-ranked option is to transfer 3 units of 8 mg/mL, 5 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would leave Corvale General with 14 days and bring Corvale East to 8 days.",
      "cites": ["D6"]
    }
  ]
}
